and was a harmless, immediately-corrected permission issue.\",\"limitations\":[\"The evidence trace does not show whether any other pre-existing CAs or trust-store entries were affected, though the update-ca-certificates output ('1 added, 0 removed') indicates no removals occurred.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"create-ca","requirement":"Create a local certificate authority named 'OS Comparison Root CA' on node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"Executor generated a 4096-bit RSA key and a self-signed x509 certificate with subject and issuer CN='OS Comparison Root CA', confirmed directly via 'openssl x509 -subject -issuer' output showing 'subject=/CN=OS Comparison Root CA' and 'issuer=/CN=OS Comparison Root CA', with a 10-year validity window.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a276d33d55324726","cmd-e20a4545055e48c9"]},{"id":"install-trusted-ca","requirement":"Install the CA certificate as a trusted system certificate authority on node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"CA cert was copied into /usr/local/share/ca-certificates and 'update-ca-certificates' reported '1 added, 0 removed; done.' Hash symlinks for the new CA were confirmed present in /etc/ssl/certs. System-wide trust was directly demonstrated by issuing a leaf certificate signed by the new CA and verifying it with plain 'openssl verify' (no -CAfile), which succeeded only because the CA is now part of the default trust bundle.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8905e3e5949f4873","cmd-21ddbc54982443d6","cmd-7ecbfdcf231f47db"]},{"id":"restart-protocol","requirement":"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol (independent of the public task contract): pre-restart baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered service/data state","status":"satisfied","summary":"Pre-restart baseline captured boot_id 8336c3a1-... plus CA file/symlink presence. 'shutdown -r now' was issued and acknowledged. Node briefly refused connections, then boot_id changed to 27295f5e-..., matching the independently capture